# A11y fixture, NO secrets: the Playwright web server boots with this; the
# scanned pages (unauthenticated surface) touch neither database nor OAuth. The
# scan stays green because session reads fail closed and the scanned routes
# never reach the database.
# Precedence: the Playwright web server starts with
# `bun --env-file=.env.a11y run start`, and `bun --env-file` only fills in keys
# the process environment has not set already, so an exported DATABASE_URL — or
# any other key below — wins over this file. From the repo root, `bun run
# test:a11y` runs `turbo run test:a11y`, whose task declares neither env nor
# passThroughEnv; turbo's strict env mode therefore strips undeclared variables
# (a CI job's DATABASE_URL among them) before Playwright starts, which leaves
# these values as the ones the server uses. Running `bun run test:a11y` from
# apps/web calls Playwright directly, without turbo, so there whatever the shell
# exported reaches the server instead.
# PORT 3100 keeps the scan clear of dev servers and other local listeners
# on 3000.
PORT=3100
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://a11y:a11y@127.0.0.1:15433/a11y_fixture
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3100
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=a11y-fixture-not-a-secret-0123456789012345
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=a11y-fixture-client-id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=a11y-fixture-client-secret
GITHUB_ALLOWED_ACCOUNT_ID=157214705
